From ec5e4da31614f8b8cde6429c647a7ad818b59d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 22:54:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add 2-Minute Lesson Loop content type (landscape, narrated)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 'authority machine' loop type — a ~2-minute landscape (16:9) real
YouTube video, not a Shorts/Reels loop, cross-posted to Facebook and
TikTok as landscape content. Script structure: hook -> 2-4 teach beats
-> worked example -> answer/explanation -> follow CTA, ~260-320 words
total narration (~100-130s spoken).

Generation follows the fast-return + background-pipeline shape already
established by lib/podcastGenerate.js (create the row as status
'generating', return its id immediately, do script+narration+background
work via runInBackground, flip to 'draft' or 'failed' when done) since a
5-8 segment script+narration job can run close to the per-invocation
time budget. New status route for the client to poll, same pattern as
/api/content-engine/podcast/status.

Narration is real per-segment TTS via the same synthesizeLine/VOICES.host_a
(Ezinne) the podcast engine already uses server-side — the local-only
edge-tts-universal path in lib/video-engine/narration.js can't run on
Vercel, see that file's own header. TTS + background search run with
the same TTS_CONCURRENCY=4 pattern as podcastGenerate.js.

Recorder (LessonLoopRecorder) plays every segment's real MP3 in sequence
and captures a live canvas+audio stream, same technique as
AudiogramRecorder (segment-advance-on-'ended' logic) fused with
QuoteLoopRecorder's background layering (video/photo/gradient, Ken Burns
on photos), just switched per-segment and landscape instead of 9:16.
Each segment gets a type badge (HOOK/KEY IDEA/EXAMPLE/ANSWER/FOLLOW), a
short on-screen keyword caption, and a subtitle band of the full
narration line for muted/sound-off viewers.

Generation also produces real per-platform metadata grounded in the
actual script (not the generic metadata-engine fallback): a genuinely
detailed YouTube title+description+tags, a conversational Facebook
caption, and a punchy TikTok caption+hashtags — surfaced in the admin
page and propagated to platform-specific content_assets rows on save.
Needs a 'lesson-loops' bucket in Supabase storage (public read,
authenticated upload) before first use. Added to AdminSidebar.
